[*] AoU layout : dv/mrp multiple resource planes (NUM_RP=2).
[*]
[*] Emphasis: what is SHARED versus what is PER-PLANE.
[*]   1. the shared link and the round-robin plane arbiter (aou_rp_arb): both
[*]      planes' in_valid, the grant, the round-robin pointer and the mid-message
[*]      lock - a fixed-priority regression shows up as a grant stuck at one plane;
[*]   2. the FDId router (aou_rp_route): the decoded FDId and BOTH per-plane RX
[*]      queues' depth/full, so a misrouted flit is visible as the wrong queue
[*]      filling;
[*]   3. per-plane Sec 6 credit banks side by side - plane 1's counters must not
[*]      move while only plane 0 is running (the no-cross-plane-leakage check);
[*]   4. the TB's own monitors (contended cycles, interleave switches, plane-1
[*]      credit movement) so the fairness/isolation verdicts have context.
[*]
[*] AXI ports are plane-sliced: bit p of each vector belongs to plane p.
[*]
[*] wave-check: env=mrp
